issue_context.body:
## Problem

Segmentation fault when argument to btree.open() is not an object.
### example code

``` Python
>>> import btree
>>> btree.open('foo')
[1]    4779 segmentation fault  ./micropython
```
## Explanation

Problem lays in argument checking inside mod_btree_open (modbtree.c:354)

``` C
    // Make sure we got a stream object
    mp_get_stream_raise(pos_args[0], MP_STREAM_OP_READ | MP_STREAM_OP_WRITE | MP_STREAM_OP_IOCTL);
```

which calls:

``` C
const mp_stream_p_t *mp_get_stream_raise(mp_obj_t self_in, int flags) {
    mp_obj_base_t *o = (mp_obj_base_t*)MP_OBJ_TO_PTR(self_in);
    const mp_stream_p_t *stream_p = o->type->protocol;
    if (stream_p == NULL
        || ((flags & MP_STREAM_OP_READ) && stream_p->read == NULL)
        || ((flags & MP_STREAM_OP_WRITE) && stream_p->write == NULL)
        || ((flags & MP_STREAM_OP_IOCTL) && stream_p->ioctl == NULL)) {
        // CPython: io.UnsupportedOperation, OSError subclass
        nlr_raise(mp_obj_new_exception_msg(&mp_type_OSError, "stream operation not supported"));
    }
    return stream_p;
}
```

This function assumes that `self_in` is always an object and it only checks if it implements a _protocol_ and if this protocol supports requested operations.

Whenever first argument for btree.open() is not an object (but a qstr for example), a non pointer dereference happens inside mp_get_stream_raise and thus causes a segfault.
## Solution

The solution is to use `MP_OBJ_IS_OBJ()` macro either before `mp_get_stream_raise()` call in mod_btree_open or inside of the mp_get_stream_raise().
### fix example:

``` Diff
diff --git a/py/stream.c b/py/stream.c
index 473eb96..81b995c 100644
--- a/py/stream.c
+++ b/py/stream.c
@@ -94,16 +94,24 @@ mp_uint_t mp_stream_rw(mp_obj_t stream, void *buf_, mp_uint_t size, int *errcode
 }

 const mp_stream_p_t *mp_get_stream_raise(mp_obj_t self_in, int flags) {
+    // check if self_in is an object before derefencing
+    if (!MP_OBJ_IS_OBJ(self_in)) {
+        goto err;
+    }
+
     mp_obj_base_t *o = (mp_obj_base_t*)MP_OBJ_TO_PTR(self_in);
     const mp_stream_p_t *stream_p = o->type->protocol;
     if (stream_p == NULL
         || ((flags & MP_STREAM_OP_READ) && stream_p->read == NULL)
         || ((flags & MP_STREAM_OP_WRITE) && stream_p->write == NULL)
         || ((flags & MP_STREAM_OP_IOCTL) && stream_p->ioctl == NULL)) {
-        // CPython: io.UnsupportedOperation, OSError subclass
-        nlr_raise(mp_obj_new_exception_msg(&mp_type_OSError, "stream operation not supported"));
+        goto err;
     }
     return stream_p;
+
+    err:
+        // CPython: io.UnsupportedOperation, OSError subclass
+        nlr_raise(mp_obj_new_exception_msg(&mp_type_OSError, "stream operation not supported"));
 }

-- 
2.7.4
```

after fix:

``` Python
>>> import btree
>>> btree.open('foo')
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "<stdin>", line 1, in <module>
OSError: stream operation not supported
```

If everyone likes this solution I can prepare a PR.
